,"for club ruffs."],["pg",""],["ls","nc"],["ls","sh"],["hs","sh"],["nt","\nSouth should next cash the top trumps "],["pg",""],["ls","sh"],["tc","c"],["pc","!ha"],["pc","!h"],["pc","!h"],["pc","!h"],["pc","!hk"],["pc","!h"],["pc","!h"],["pc","!s"],["pc","!hq"],["pc","!h"],["pc","!d"],["pc","!s"],["tc","r"],["hs","wh"],["at","revealing that West began with a certain trump trick. "],["pg",""],["ls","wh"],["hs","sh"],["at","South is now at the crossroads. If he chooses to play for a squeeze, he should surrender a trump trick at once. "],["pg",""],["ls","sh"],["pc","h"],["pc","h"],["pc","d"],["pc","d"],["pg",""],["hs","ed"],["hs","ec"],["at","If East began with 4 or more diamonds along with 5 or more clubs, "],["pg",""],["ls","ec"],["ls","ed"],["hs","ss"],["hs","ns"],["at","he can later be simple squeezed (or trump squeezed) on the run of the spades."],["pg",""],["ls","ss"],["ls","ns"],["up","4"],["md","0,ct9,,std8"],["hs","nc"],["hs","sh"],["nt","\nSouth gives himself slightly better odds, however, by playing to ruff all of dummy's clubs. "],["pg",""],["ls","nc"],["ls","sh"],["hs","ws"],["hs","wh"],["hs","wd"],["hs","wc"],["at","West must have either 3415 "],["pg",""],["md","0,d8,,c9"],["at","or 3424 distribution for this line to succeed. "],["pg",""],["ls","ws"],["ls","wh"],["ls","wd"],["ls","wc"],["hs","ss"],["hs","ns"],["at","South should begin by cashing 3 rounds of spades ending in the dummy. "],["pg",""],["ls","ss"],["ls","ns"],["tc","c"],["pc","!sk"],["pc","!s"],["pc","!s"],["pc","!s"],["pc","!sq"],["pc","!s"],["pc","!s"],["pc","!s"],["pc","!s"],["pc","!s"],["pc","!sa"],["pc","!d9"],["tc","r"],["hs","nc"],["hs","sh"],["at","A second club is ruffed."],["pg",""],["ls","sh"],["ls","nc"],["pc","c"],["pc","ck"],["pc","h"],["pc","c"],["pg",""],["hc","da"],["nt","\nSouth cashes the @DA "],["pg",""],["lc","da"],["pc","da"],["pc","d"],["pc","d"],["pc","d"],["pg",""],["hs","sd"],["at","and continues a low diamond. "],["pg",""],["ls","sd"],["pc","d"],["md","0,c9,,d8"],["hs","wd"],["at","If West began with a singleton diamond, "],["pg",""],["ls","wd"],["hs","wh"],["at","it will not help him to ruff "],["pg",""],["ls","wh"],["hs","ss"],["hs","ns"],["at","(notice that if all of the spades had not been cashed earlier, West could defeat the contract by pitching a spade on the second diamond)."],["pg",""],["ls","ss"],["ls","ns"],["hc","dk"],["nt","\nAfter dummy wins the @DK, "],["pg",""],["lc","dk"],["pc","c"],["pc","dk"],["pc","d"],["pg",""],["hs","nc"],["hs","sh"],["at","South leads dummy's last club and ruffs in the closed hand. "],["pg",""],["ls","nc"],["ls","sh"],["pc","c"],["pc","d"],["pc","h"],["pc","c"],["pg",""],["hs","wh"],["hs","ed"],["at","West is forced to ruff his partner's diamond winner at trick 13."],["pg",""],["ls","wh"],["ls","ed"],["nt","\nThe mathematics required to choose between the 2 lines of play are too complex for almost anyone to solve at the table. The odds of success of the 2 lines are very close but the \"ruffing line\" does give slightly better odds than the \"squeeze line\"."],["",""]]}}